vendor/zip: use the largefile-aware stat in zip_mkpath()

zip_mkpath() declares st as struct MZ_FILE_STAT_STRUCT, which is
struct stat64 under -D_LARGEFILE64_SOURCE -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 (always
passed by the Buildroot glibc toolchain), but then calls the plain lstat()
on it. GCC rejects this as incompatible-pointer-types, so the build fails.

Use MZ_FILE_STAT(), as the stat() call at the top of the same function
already does.

--- a/vendor/zip/src/zip.c
+++ b/vendor/zip/src/zip.c
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@
         *p = '/';
       }
 
-      if (lstat(npath, &st) < 0) {
+      if (MZ_FILE_STAT(npath, &st) < 0) {
         if (MZ_MKDIR(npath) == -1) {
           if (errno != EEXIST) {
             return ZIP_EMKDIR;
